# YubiKey PIV authentication (slot 9A).
#
# Identities come from ssh-agent, which has the PKCS#11 module loaded
# (see ~/.config/systemd/user/ssh-agent.service and `yk-reload`).
#
# Deliberately NO PKCS11Provider line here. Loading the module in both the
# agent and ssh opens two competing PIV sessions on the token; the direct load
# evicts the agent's cached PIN and signing then fails with
# "agent refused operation".
#
# IdentityFile + IdentitiesOnly are kept on purpose: the token exposes SEVEN
# keys over PKCS#11 (slot 9A, five age-plugin-yubikey retired slots,
# attestation) and the agent offers all of them. That is one MORE than the
# default MaxAuthTries of 6, so without IdentitiesOnly a server can reject the
# connection before ssh ever reaches slot 9A -- and which keys get tried first
# is not something this end controls. IdentitiesOnly restricts what is offered
# to the identities listed here; it applies to agent-provided keys too, not
# just files, so it still works without PKCS11Provider.
#
# Counted with `ssh-add -l` against the loaded agent. It was six when this was
# written; a retired slot has been added since. If it grows again the margin
# does not get worse -- IdentitiesOnly already caps what is offered at one --
# but the number in this comment should be re-checked rather than trusted.

Host *
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_yubikey_piv.pub
    IdentitiesOnly yes

Host github.com
    User git

Host gitlab.com
    User git
